    "description": "Mosaic Forest Management is a timberlands management company overseeing large private forestlands and associated public tenures on Vancouver Island and coastal British Columbia. The platform serves timber, lumber, and broader forest-products markets through harvesting, stewardship, and land-management activities. Its operating model is asset-heavy because it manages extensive timberlands where value is tied to land quality, biological growth, harvest planning, and log sales. Company materials describe Mosaic as the manager for the TimberWest and Island Timberlands ownership interests and note a supply chain supporting roughly 2,000 employees and contractors. Operations are concentrated in British Columbia, particularly on Vancouver Island and the province's coast. Mosaic launched in 2018 as the management platform for TimberWest and Island Timberlands; BCI's 2024 I&RR financial statements disclose a 56.1% ownership interest in Mosaic LP, while public materials also identify PSP Investments as an underlying ownership partner.",
